            <ArticleTitle>[One case of giant hypopharyngeal and esophageal inflammtory fibroid polyp].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>663-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical manifestations of the disease include dysphagia, foreign body sensation in pharyngeal, retrosternal pain and regurgitation. Physical examination showed a sausage-shaped mass hanging outside the mouth, sometimes. CT scan demonstrated a benign placeholder in upper segment of esophagus. Surgery is the only way to achieve radical cure. Pathological examination: inflammtory fibroid polyp.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
